WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
The airframe supports the aircraft's structure and payload.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.500
Motors and propellers generate lift and control movement.

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:09.500
Damage, incorrect installation, contamination, or imbalance can affect stability,

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:12.445
so these components require inspection before and after flight.

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:14.990
Batteries supply high power under changing loads.

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:16.990
Their charge, temperature, condition, age,

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:20.190
and storage practices influence flight time and reliability.

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:24.260
Battery estimates are planning inputs, not guarantees; wind, payload, maneuvering,

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:25.945
and temperature can change consumption.

00:00:25.945 --> 00:00:29.425
The flight controller combines operator commands with sensor data to stabilize the

00:00:29.425 --> 00:00:29.995
aircraft.

00:00:29.995 --> 00:00:33.700
GPS and other navigation sensors may support position hold, navigation,

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:34.990
and return functions.

00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:39.500
Sensor error, interference, obstruction, or configuration can reduce those capabilities.

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:42.030
Cameras, thermal sensors, mapping equipment,

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:46.010
and other payloads create mission value but add weight, power demand, complexity,

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:47.500
and data-handling requirements.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:50.485
A payload must be securely mounted, compatible with the aircraft,

00:00:50.485 --> 00:00:52.490
and appropriate for the lawful mission.

00:00:52.490 --> 00:00:56.495
The ground-control station may be a dedicated controller, mobile device, or computer.

00:00:56.495 --> 00:01:00.000
Telemetry links carry command, status, position, and sometimes video.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.990
Link quality depends on distance, obstacles, interference, orientation, and system design.

00:01:04.990 --> 00:01:09.450
Firmware and mobile applications coordinate aircraft behavior, settings, maps, accounts,

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:10.000
and records.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.995
Keep approved software maintained, understand significant changes, protect accounts,

00:01:13.995 --> 00:01:15.970
and confirm configuration before flight.

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:19.500
No single automated feature replaces operator awareness and judgment.
